  "id": "BIT-phpmyadmin-2026-119428",
  "summary": "phpMyAdmin through 5.2.3 SSRF via setup/validate.php After Setup Disabled",
  "details": "phpMyAdmin through 5.2.3 contains a server-side request forgery vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to trigger outbound connections via setup/validate.php, which lacks the setup-disabled guard. Attackers can POST attacker-chosen host and port values reaching Validator::testDBConnection() to open MySQL-protocol connections and probe internal ports using returned error messages.",
